  "body": "## What\n\nv5.24.0 and v5.25.0 shipped `anthropic` and `anthropic_oauth`, and **no user-facing document mentioned either**. This closes that, and fixes four stale provider counts found on the way.\n\n## Four stale counts, one release\n\n| Where | Was | Now |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| README intro | 54 | 56 |\n| README Features table | 54 | 56 |\n| `docs/USAGE.md` §1 | 54 | 56 |\n| `docs/USAGE.md` §7 | 54 | 56 |\n\n`test_readme_provider_table_covers_full_catalog` pins the provider **table** against `PROVIDER_CATALOG` and caught none of these — a prose count is not the table. Same shape as §72, where a target guard didn't protect the sentence beside the target.\n\n## What was added\n\n- **README** — a Features row for Claude-direct, plus an Anthropic subsection under the existing `## OAuth Providers` heading (not a new top-level section).\n- **`docs/USAGE.md`** — a \"Using Claude models\" subsection under Providers, with its own anchor and TOC entry. Existing anchors untouched (§129).\n- **In-dashboard Guide** — a `guide-claude-models` section with a TOC entry, because that's where users actually read this.\n\nAll three say the same two things: `anthropic` with a Console key is the ordinary supported path; `anthropic_oauth` is **not permitted by Anthropic**, has no \"inside Claude Code\" exemption, and is gated by default to `cc_entrypoint=cli`.\n\n## The Guide edit nearly shipped broken, twice\n\n1. **I invented `guide-callout` / `guide-callout-warn`** — neither exists in `admin.css`. Per §66, an unstyled class is not an error: the disclaimer would have rendered as flat prose with no visual weight and **nothing would have failed**. Now reuses `.guide-note` with a new `.guide-note-warn` modifier defined beside its base class.\n2. **The warn colour is border-and-fill only, never body text.** §144 measured `--warn` as text at **4.1:1** on the light theme — under AA. The rule sets `border-left-color` and `background` and leaves prose on the neutral token, with the reason in a CSS comment so it doesn't get \"improved\" later.\n\nChecked mechanically before any browser: every class the new section emits has a CSS rule, every `#guide-*` anchor resolves to a real id, and every `var(--token)` in the diff is declared.\n\n## New guards — and these aren't label checks\n\n`anthropic_oauth` uses a credential in a way Anthropic's terms forbid, and the only thing between a user and an account-level consequence is that the docs say so. A future edit trimming the warning \"for brevity\" would leave the provider shipped and the disclaimer gone.\n\n```\nthe disclaimer exists and still says \"does not permit\"\nevery doc that offers the provider links the disclaimer\nthe Guide renders it as a warning (guide-note-warn), not as prose\n```\n\n**All three confirmed to fail by name** (§134):\n\n```\n\"does not permit\" -> \"discourages\"   -> disclaimer test FAILED\ndelete ANTHROPIC-SUBSCRIPTION.md     -> disclaimer test FAILED\nguide-note-warn  -> guide-note       -> guide test FAILED\n```\n\n**When a feature's safety rests on a sentence, put a test on the sentence.**\n\n## Verification\n\n| Layer | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Full suite | **4214 passed**, 26 skipped |\n| Failures | **6**, all `tests/scripts/test_installers.py` PowerShell — documented irreducible baseline, identical to unmodified `main` |\n| ruff format / check / ty / suppression grep | clean |\n\n## Version\n\nBumped **PATCH** (5.25.0 → 5.25.1): the Guide lives under `src/my_claude_code/api/`, a production path per CLAUDE.md, so a bump is required even though the change is documentation content with no behaviour change.\n\n## Residual\n\n- The Guide section was verified structurally (classes, anchors, tokens) but **not opened in a browser** — no server was started for this docs pass. Layout and contrast of the new callout are reasoned-about, not measured.\n- Pre-existing and untouched: the README and Guide still don't document the 504-setting Claude Code config editor or image analytics (carried debt).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
