   "body": "## Browser verification — the residual risk is now closed\n\nI listed \"verified structurally but not opened in a browser\" as a residual. That's no longer true; a throwaway server on :8191 (fake `HOME`, live :8082 never touched) confirms it.\n\n**Composited contrast of the callout prose, all four themes** — alpha composited down to the first opaque ancestor (§144), transitions disabled before measuring (§141):\n\n| Theme | Prose contrast | Border colour | Border width |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Midnight | **17.97:1** | `rgb(245,158,11)` | 3px |\n| Paper (light) | **17.28:1** | `rgb(180,83,9)` | 3px |\n| High Contrast | **21.00:1** | `rgb(255,212,0)` | 3px |\n| Velvet | **15.61:1** | `rgb(245,176,65)` | 3px |\n\nThat is the border-and-fill decision paying off: §144 measured `--warn` **as text** at 4.1:1 on the light theme, under AA. Keeping prose on the neutral token puts every theme between 15.6:1 and 21:1, and the structure is identical across all four (§127 — a callout that changes shape per theme reads as broken).\n\nAlso confirmed live:\n\n```\nsection renders + visible          true\nTOC entry present                  true (15 entries)\ncallout resolves .guide-note-warn  bg rgba(245,158,11,0.08), border-left rgb(245,158,11)\n\"not permitted\" in the section     true\n\"cc_entrypoint=cli\" in the section true\nno console errors                  true\n```\n\nCleanup checked with receipts: :8191 re-probed `000` (gone), live :8082 `200`, no `anthropic_oauth.json` or onboarding state written into the real `~/.fcc` (§55c), throwaway home removed.\n\nOne thing I noticed and did **not** chase: the action bar shows \"1 unsaved change\" on a fresh throwaway home with no `.env`. That reproduces independently of this change and is a throwaway-home artifact, not something this PR introduced.",
