    "message": "docs: document both Anthropic providers across README, USAGE and the Guide\n\nv5.24.0 and v5.25.0 shipped `anthropic` and `anthropic_oauth` and no\nuser-facing document mentioned either. This closes that, and fixes four stale\nprovider counts found on the way.\n\nTwo providers shipped and four separate hardcoded counts went stale in one\nsession: the README intro, the README Features table, and two places in\nUSAGE.md all still said 54. `test_readme_provider_table_covers_full_catalog`\npins the provider *table* against PROVIDER_CATALOG and caught none of them,\nbecause a prose count is not the table -- the same shape as the target guard in\n§72 that did not protect the sentence beside the target.\n\nWhat was added, each where it belongs:\n\n- README: a Features row for Claude-direct, and an Anthropic subsection under\n  the existing `## OAuth Providers` heading rather than a new top-level one.\n- docs/USAGE.md: a \"Using Claude models\" subsection under Providers, with its\n  own anchor and TOC entry; existing anchors untouched.\n- The in-dashboard Guide: a `guide-claude-models` section with a TOC entry,\n  because the dashboard is where a user actually reads this.\n\nAll three explain the same two things: `anthropic` with a Console key is the\nordinary supported path, and `anthropic_oauth` is not permitted by Anthropic,\nwith no \"inside Claude Code\" exemption, gated by default to `cc_entrypoint=cli`.\n\nThe Guide edit nearly shipped broken twice. I first invented `guide-callout` /\n`guide-callout-warn`, neither of which exists in admin.css -- §66: an unstyled\nclass is not an error, so the disclaimer would have rendered as flat prose and\nnothing would have failed. It now reuses `.guide-note` with a new\n`.guide-note-warn` modifier. That modifier puts the warn colour on the border\nand the fill only and leaves prose on the neutral text token, because §144\nmeasured `--warn` as text at 4.1:1 on the light theme, under AA; the reason is\nin the CSS comment so it does not get \"improved\" later.\n\nChecked mechanically before any browser: every class the new section emits has\na CSS rule, every `#guide-*` anchor resolves to a real id, and every\n`var(--token)` in the diff is declared.\n\nNew guards in test_docs_ui_labels.py, which are not label checks. This provider\nuses a credential in a way Anthropic's terms forbid, and the only thing between\na user and an account-level consequence is that the docs say so:\n\n- the disclaimer exists and still says \"does not permit\"\n- every doc offering the provider links the disclaimer\n- the Guide renders it as a warning, not as ordinary prose\n\nAll three confirmed to fail by name against three mutations: softening \"does\nnot permit\" to \"discourages\", deleting the file, and downgrading the Guide\ncallout. When a feature's safety rests on a sentence, put a test on the\nsentence.\n\nVerification: full suite 4214 passed, 26 skipped, 6 failures -- all\ntests/scripts/test_installers.py PowerShell, the documented irreducible\nbaseline, identical to unmodified fork/main. ruff format, ruff check, ty and\nthe suppression grep all clean.\n\nVersion bumped PATCH because the Guide lives under src/my_claude_code/api/,\nwhich is a production path; the change is documentation content with no\nbehaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
